wly pushes in.\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, cut to medium-to-close shot: <Subject 1> picks up the complete mooncake <Subject 3> from the ceramic plate with both hands and shows it to the camera; then snaps it apart with force — the mooncake instantly splits into two complete halves with a clean, flat break, no stickiness, no stringy pull, as crisp as breaking a thin biscuit; a few dry crumbs fall from the broken edges; the camera pushes in on the split cross-section <Subject 4>, the black-sesame and pine-nut filling stays loose and grainy with slight crumble. At 00:05.500, (S1) says in the same warm voice: <d>[zh] 层层起酥，黑芝麻松仁馅。</d>\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, cut to a close-up: <Subject 1> holds the split half mooncake <Subject 4> in one hand, steps forward happily one or two steps toward the camera and stops; she extends the half mooncake toward the camera as if inviting the viewer outside the frame to taste it, making a cute inviting expression - bright eyes, gentle smile; her face and the half mooncake are in the same frame, warm and heart-warming. At 00:10.500, (S1) says in a cute warm inviting tone: <d>[zh] 来，请你尝一口！</d> Then a warm freeze frame, gentle fade out.\nThe girl's warm natural Asian skin tone and exposure stay identical throughout; the mooncake is EXACTLY ONE whole mooncake split into two halves - no extra pieces, no missing parts; no extra people, no extra props; no text, no logo, no watermark, no embedded subtitles.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nTraditional teahouse ambience throughout: gentle ceramic tea-cup clinks, faint water boiling, distant soft murmurs; a crisp, light snapping sound when the crust breaks.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nWarm guochao-style background music (guzheng and pipa with light percussion), slow gentle tempo, low volume so the voice-over stays clear; one track consistent across the whole 15s film, ending with a soft, warm resolution."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name